 "about": "The street furniture DGT's LiDAR finds (tools/furniture.mjs, task 100), checked against the photos: each piece of the LiDAR's that a viewpoint's photo or a reference photo (refs/photos.json) shows within 50 m, not behind a building, drawn at random (tools/furniture.mjs mark) and looked at by a session in that photo. checks: every piece looked at, at: where the tiles have it; kind: what the LiDAR said it is; photo: the photo; round: which drawing it was in (1 and 2 were before the rules were last changed, and those the rules no longer find are kept here but out of the sample); seen: 'right' (it's what the kind says), 'other' (a piece of street furniture of another kind: a lamp post where it says a sign, a sign board), 'wrong' (no furniture there: a parapet, a tree, a glass front, wires), 'unsure' (the photo doesn't show it: out of its frame or too small); what: what the photo shows there. sample: the 50 the tiles still have, and how many of each. faces: the signs whose face a photo shows (read, not drawn: task 082), which tools/furniture.mjs takes before its guess. The photos are from 2010 to 2025 and the LiDAR from July 2025, so a piece can have come or gone between them. low: the benches, bins and bollards found by size in an earlier version of the rules (a bench's seat 0.35 to 0.95 m up and 1.3 to 2.4 m long, a container's lid 1 to 1.7 m up and 0.9 to 2.3 m long, posts 0.55 to 1.3 m high in a row), drawn and looked at the same way: none was one, so tools/furniture.mjs no longer looks for them.",
